WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.400
When it comes to something
as life-and-death important

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.120
as what to feed ourselves
and our families,

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.760
we should rely not on
anecdotes, but on facts.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.080
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:21.720
The liver is a crucial organ in the body,
playing a vital role in metabolism,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.120
detoxification, digestion,
blood sugar regulation,

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.680
and vitamin storage.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:31.520
Today we start with a story about the
liver damage caused by Herbalife supplements.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.840
Herbalife is
a multi-billion-dollar,

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.560
multi-level
marketing supplement company

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.640
that was forced to pay
hundreds of millions of dollars

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.320
to settle charges of deception
and corrupt business practices.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.640
It also holds the distinction
of being the dietary supplement

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.400
most frequently implicated

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.200
in injuring
the livers of consumers.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.480
Herbal does not mean innocuous.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.320
Cases of severe liver toxicity

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.000
associated
with Herbalife supplements

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.680
started to be published in 2007
around the world.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.520
As the accompanying
editorial summarized,

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.000
there were 22 cases
of liver damage

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.840
following Herbalife intake
in the first two reports,

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.360
with two patients developing
fulminant liver failure

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.840
requiring liver transplantation.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.960
Only one survived.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:22.800
The editorial concluded
that this clearly shifts

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.640
the risk-benefit ratio
against its use.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.040
Maybe it's contaminated
with chemicals or heavy metals,

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:33.800
maybe due to contamination
with a liver toxic bacteria

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.160
found in implicated products.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.800
Additional reports
continued to be published,

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:39.960
followed by rebuttals

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.280
written by Herbalife
company representatives

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.760
questioning cause-and-effect.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.120
No small task,

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.120
given that people were taking

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.880
up to 17 different
Herbalife products at one time.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.880
So how strong is the evidence?

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.360
A key factor to look for
is re-challenge tests

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.120
or "positive re-exposure."

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.880
Did someone decide
to take the product again

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:06.440
after the initial
liver injury resolved,

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.800
and did their symptoms return
on re-challenge?

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.640
Based on stringent
causality assessment methods

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.560
like positive re-exposure tests,

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.920
cause-and-effect
is considered probable

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.960
for at least
a few Herbalife products.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.760
They are such
a moving target, though,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:25.000
with "hundreds of different
products marketed globally

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.000
in over 88 markets,
where in many cases

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.840
the formula is
unique to a region..."

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.600
Positive rechallenge cases
continue to be published,

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.120
confirming the toxic cause
of liver damage

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.840
from Herbalife products,

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.000
perhaps by triggering
an autoimmune reaction.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.640
This fatal case
of a 24-year-old woman

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.000
was attributed
to Herbalife products,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.960
which were evidently found
to contain heavy metals,

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.080
traces of a psychotropic
recreational agent,

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.440
and pathogenic bacteria.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.840
The paper was subsequently
taken down for "legal reasons"

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.320
after legal threats
by Herbalife.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.920
LiverTox is a federal initiative

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:07.720
between the National
Institutes of Health

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.520
and the National
Library of Medicine

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.920
to categorize the likelihood

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.720
that substances
can damage the liver,

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:18.440
all the way up to the highest
likelihood—Category A—

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.840
meaning it is a well-known,
well-described,

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.080
and well-reported
cause of liver damage.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:26.560
And that's exactly
how it characterized

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.160
Herbalife supplements:

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.760
A well-established cause

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.920
of clinically apparent
liver injury.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:34.680
In our next story,

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:39.441
we look at the dietary factors
that can contribute to liver disease.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:45.480
In the documentary, Supersize Me, Morgan Spurlock
eats exclusively at McDonald's for a month,

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.920
and predictably his weight, blood
pressure, and cholesterol go up,

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.760
but so do his liver enzymes,

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:57.480
a sign his liver cells are dying and spilling
their contents into the bloodstream.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:01.120
His one-man experiment was
actually formally replicated.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:05.280
A group of men and women agreed to eat
two fast food meals a day for a month,

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:10.160
and most of their liver values started
out normal, under 30 here for men,

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.560
but within just one week,
most were out of whack,

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:18.840
a profound pathological
elevation in liver damage.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:25.000
What's happening is NAFLD,
non-alcoholic fatty liver disease,

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.160
the next global epidemic.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.760
Fatty deposits in the liver can result
in a disease spectrum —

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:38.160
from asymptomatic fat buildup,
to NASH, nonalcoholic steatohepatitis,

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.680
which can lead to liver
scarring and cirrhosis,

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:44.680
which can result in liver cancer,
liver failure, and death.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:50.360
It's now the most common cause
of chronic liver disease in the U.S.,

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:55.280
affecting 70 million Americans —
that's like one in three adults.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.160
And fast food is a great
way to bring it on,

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:04.480
since it's associated with the
intake of soft drinks and meat.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.720
One can of soda a day may raise
the odds of fatty liver 45%,

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:12.160
and those eating the equivalent of 14
chicken nuggets worth of meat a day

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:17.520
have nearly triple the rates of fatty liver
compared to like seven nuggets or less.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:24.000
It's been characterized as a tale of fat
and sugar, but evidently not all types of fat.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.800
Those with fatty hepatitis ate
more animal fat and cholesterol,

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.840
and less plant fat, fiber, and
antioxidants, which may explain

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:36.400
why adherence to a Mediterranean-style
diet, characterized by high consumption

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.480
of foods such as fruits, vegetables,
whole grains, and beans

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:43.560
is associated with less severe
non-alcoholic fatty liver disease,

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:49.040
perhaps because of the anti-inflammatory
and antioxidant effects.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:54.080
Maybe because of specific phytonutrients,
like the purple, red, blue anthocyanin

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:59.640
pigments in berries and grapes, and plums,
red cabbage, red onions, radicchio.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:04.840
These anthocyanin-rich foods may be
promising for the prevention of fatty liver,

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.400
but that's mostly based
on Petri dish experiments.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:13.320
There was one clinical trial that did find
that drinking a purple sweet potato

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:17.960
beverage seemed to successfully
dampen liver inflammation though.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.800
A more plant-based diet may
also improve our microbiome,

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:25.160
the good bacteria in our gut. The
old adage, "we are what we eat"

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:28.920
may be changing to "we are
what our bacteria eat."

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:33.800
And when we eat fat, we may
facilitate the growth of bad bacteria,

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:36.600
which can release inflammatory
molecules that increase

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:42.440
the leakiness of our gut and
contribute to fatty liver disease.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:49.240
Fatty liver disease can also be
caused by cholesterol overload.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:53.800
The thought is that dietary cholesterol
found in eggs, meat, and dairy

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.720
oxidizes and then up-regulates
liver X receptor alpha,

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.840
which can up-regulate something
else called SREBP,

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:04.440
which can increase the
level of fat in the liver.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:09.200
Cholesterol crystals alone cause
human white blood cells to spill out

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.560
inflammatory compounds, just
like uric acid crystals in gout.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:18.560
That's what may be triggering the
progression of just plain fatty liver

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.120
into serious hepatitis,

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:25.120
the accumulation of sufficient
concentrations of free cholesterol

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:29.760
within fatty liver cells to cause
crystallization of the cholesterol-

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:34.320
one of several recent lines of evidence
suggesting that dietary cholesterol plays

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:40.520
an important role in the development
of fatty hepatitis, fatty liver inflammation.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:44.640
In a study of 9,000 American
adults followed for 13 years,

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:48.280
they found a strong association
between dietary cholesterol intake

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:54.040
and hospitalization and death
from cirrhosis and liver cancer,

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:59.440
as dietary cholesterol can oxidize and
cause toxic and carcinogenic effects.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:04.800
To limit the toxicity of excess
cholesterol derived from the diet,

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.120
the liver tries to rid itself of cholesterol
by dumping it into the bloodstream,

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:12.600
and so by measuring the
non-HDL cholesterol in the blood

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:16.280
one can predict the onset
of fatty liver disease.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:21.120
If you subtract HDL from total cholesterol,
none of the hundreds of people

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:25.560
they followed with a value under
130 developed the disease.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:29.440
Drug companies view non-alcoholic
fatty liver disease as a bonanza,

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:34.360
as is the case of any disease of
affluence, considering its already high

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:39.360
and raising prevalence, needing
continuous pharmacologic treatment.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:42.840
But maybe it's as easy
as changing our diet,

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:47.280
avoiding sugary and
cholesterol-laden foods.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.520
The unpalatable truth is that
non-alcoholic fatty liver disease

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.280
could almost be considered the
human equivalent of foie gras,

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:59.440
as we "force-feed" ourselves foods that
can result in serious health implications.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:04.080
However, having such a buttery
texture in human livers

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:08.800
is not a delicacy to be enjoyed by
liver doctors in clinical practice

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:12.840
as it can have such
serious consequences.

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:13.760
Finally today,

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:17.120
did you know that cancer-
causing viruses in poultry

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.920
may explain increased risks of death
from liver and pancreatic cancers?

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.960
Here’s the story.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:28.200
Thousands of Americans continue
to die from asbestos exposure

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.720
decades after many
uses were banned

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.800
because the cancers can
take years to show up.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:37.440
We are now in the so-called third
wave of asbestos related disease.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:40.840
The first wave was in
the asbestos miners,

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.400
which started in the 1920s.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:44.600
The second phase
was in the workers—

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.520
the ship-builders and
construction workers

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:49.720
that used the stuff in
the 30s, 40s, and 50s.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:52.640
Now as "buildings constructed
with asbestos"

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:56.680
"over the past six decades begin
to age and deteriorate”,

00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:58.400
not only are
workers at risk,

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:02.080
but "Potential also exists for
serious environmental exposure"

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.480
"to asbestos among residents, tenants
and users of these buildings"

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:10.960
"such as school children, office workers,
maintenance workers, and the general public.”

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.080
The CDC, the American
Academy of Pediatrics,

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.600
and the EPA "have projected
that over the next 30 years"

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:20.640
"approximately 1,000 cases of
mesothelioma and lung cancer "

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.480
"will occur among persons
in the United States"

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:27.960
"exposed to asbestos in school
buildings as school children."

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:31.000
But it all started
with the workers.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:35.440
As one internal industry
memo callously put it,

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:41.160
"If you've enjoyed a good life while working
with asbestos products why not die from it."

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.440
To see if something
is carcinogenic,

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:46.400
you study those who have
the most exposure.

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:47.800
That's how we learned
about the potential

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:50.160
cancer-causing
dangers of asbestos,

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.720
and that's how we're
learning about

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:55.880
the potential cancer-causing
dangers of poultry viruses.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.640
For years I've talked about
the excess mortality

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:01.760
in poultry workers associated
with these wart-causing

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.520
chicken cancer viruses
that may be transmitted

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:10.040
to those in the general population
handling fresh or frozen chicken.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:13.320
Last year I talked about the largest
study to date, at the time,

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:15.520
confirming the findings
of three other studies

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.160
“that workers in poultry slaughtering
and processing plants"

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:21.640
"have increased risk of
dying from certain cancers”,

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:24.480
and adding death
from penis cancer

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:28.240
to the risks linked
to poultry exposure.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:30.400
That was looking at
20,000 poultry workers.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:35.240
Well, we have yet another study,
looking at 30,000.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.520
The purpose of
the study was to

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:39.760
"test the hypothesis that exposure
to poultry (cancer) viruses"

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.800
"that widely occurs occupationally
in poultry workers"

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:45.840
not to mention the
general population,

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:49.000
"may be associated with
increased risks of deaths"

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:52.040
"from liver and
pancreatic cancers."

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.560
They found that those
who slaughter chickens

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:58.880
have about 9 times the odds of both
pancreatic cancer and liver cancer.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.160
Just to put this in context,

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:02.840
the most carefully studied risk
factor for pancreatic cancer,

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:06.360
one of our deadliest cancers,
is cigarette smoking.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:09.800
Even if you smoke for more
than 50 years, though,

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:12.880
you only about double your
odds of pancreatic cancer.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:14.480
Those that slaughter
poultry appear to have

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:17.080
nearly 9 times the odds.

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:20.600
For liver cancer,
it's more alcohol.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.520
Those that consume more
than a four drinks a day

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:25.200
have triple odds of lung cancer,

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.920
whereas poultry slaughtering appears

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:29.520
to increase one's odds 9 fold.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:32.120
There are diseases unique
to the meat industry,

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:35.400
like the newly described
"salami brusher's disease"

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:38.960
that affects those whose job
it is to wire brush off

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.800
the white mold that
naturally grows on salami,

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:43.680
for 8 hours a day,

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:48.600
but most diseases suffered by
meat workers are more universal.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:51.640
The reason the connection
between asbestos and cancer

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:53.440
was so easy to
nail down is that

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:57.760
asbestos caused a particularly
unusual cancer,

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:00.080
which was virtually
unknown until there was

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:03.400
widespread asbestos mining
and industrial use.

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:06.800
But the pancreatic cancer one
might get from handling chicken,

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:10.320
is the same pancreatic cancer one
might get from smoking cigarettes,

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:14.400
so it's more difficult to tease out
a cause-and-effect relationship.

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:18.600
So don't expect to see
an asbestos-type ban

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:24.000
on Kentucky Fried Chicken
anytime soon.

